E AX3047 496-sized-integer-type.ax:19:11-14 sized-integer-type "`u64` is a type variable spelling, not an Axiom primitive" #"use the Axiom primitive type name" ?"Write `UInt64`. Primitive type names begin with a capital letter. Int is signed 64-bit; Int8, Int16, Int32, UInt8, UInt16, UInt32 and UInt64 carry distinct precision and signedness. Convert explicitly with `(as value Type)`; lowercase primitive spellings cannot stand in for these types."
